stance (120&amp;quot;)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;7&#39;9&amp;quot;-13&#39;0&amp;quot; (9&#39;9&amp;quot;)&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;8&#39;7&amp;quot;-17&#39;5&amp;quot; (11&#39;6&amp;quot;)&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;11&#39;9&amp;quot;-18&#39;8&amp;quot; (14&#39;5&amp;quot;)&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;11&#39;9&amp;quot;-24&#39;8&amp;quot; (15&#39;11&amp;quot;)&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lens Shift&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;Vertical&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;Horizontal/Vertical&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;Horizontal/Vertical&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;Horizontal/Vertical&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Brightness&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;3500 Lumens&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;7000 Lumens&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;2000 Lumens&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;2700 Lumens&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contrast Ratio&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;4000:1 (15,000:1 Dynamic)&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;10,000:1 (100,000:1 Dynamic)&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;40,000:1&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;(2,500,000:1 Dynamic)&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Color Gamut&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;110% of BT.2020&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;110% of BT.2020&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;93% of DCI-P3&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;87% of DCI-P3&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HDR&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;HDR10+, DV, HLG, IMAX E&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;HDR10+, DV, HLG, IMAX E&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;HDR10+, Dynamic HDR Tone Mapping&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;HDR10+, HLG&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Size&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;10.20&amp;quot; x 7.30&amp;quot; x 9.20&amp;quot;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;14.9&amp;quot; x 11.3&amp;quot; x 9.1&amp;quot;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;17.7&amp;quot; x 8.2&amp;quot; x 18.9&amp;quot;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;7.60&amp;quot; x 20.50&amp;quot; x 17.60&amp;quot;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Weight&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;16.5 lbs&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;17.9 lbs&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;32.2 lbs&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;28 lbs&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Misc&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;TRUE native 4k&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;td&gt;No dynamic tone mapping&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The JVC seems to be the most all-around popular. The Valerion seems really nice, but not as mature. The JVC, despite its lower lumens, is touted as having better blacks and color contrast. It also is the only one that does native 4k rather than using pixel shifting like the others. Also the dynamic HDR tone mapping is highly touted.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Screen Frame</title>
				<link>//localhost:1313/posts/06---projects/house/basement/theater-construction/resources/screen-frame/</link>
				<pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 00:52:43 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>//localhost:1313/posts/06---projects/house/basement/theater-construction/resources/screen-frame/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;ideal&#34;&gt;Ideal&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Taken from BIGmouthinDC (thread &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.avsforum.com/threads/minimalist-approach-to-screen-wall.837848/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noreferrer nofollow&#34;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;). Build a basic frame (include a bottom horizontal bar too, probably). This will support the screen.&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;p class=&#34;imgp&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/ob/99%20-%20Attachments/Pasted%20image%2020260909195251.png&#34; alt=&#34;Pasted image 20260909195251.png&#34;  /&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Then for the gaps on the sides/top/bottom, can build small frames with fabric:&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;p class=&#34;imgp&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/ob/99%20-%20Attachments/Pasted%20image%2020260909195612.png&#34; alt=&#34;Pasted image 20260909195612.png&#34;  /&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In these builds he just friction fits the panels around the screen. Maybe a small furrowing side on the left/right. Maybe some velcro to hold them in place.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;more-pics&#34;&gt;More Pics&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;p class=&#34;imgp&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/ob/99%20-%20Attachments/Pasted%20image%2020260910071524.png&#34; alt=&#34;Pasted image 20260910071524.png&#34;  /&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Flooring</title>
				<link>//localhost:1313/posts/06---projects/house/basement/theater-construction/flooring/</link>
				<pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 18:33:10 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>//localhost:1313/posts/06---projects/house/basement/theater-construction/flooring/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;overview&#34;&gt;Overview&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Carpet&amp;hellip;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;soundproofing&#34;&gt;Soundproofing&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;May not be as important since its just a concrete slab, but that can still carry some low frequency sound. Could consider something easy like a sound absorption mat (like &lt;a href=&#34;https://shop.soundproofingcompany.com/collections/soundproofing-essentials/products/serena-mat-underlay&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noreferrer nofollow&#34;&gt;this&lt;/a&gt;) placed directly on the slab:&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;p class=&#34;imgp&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/ob/99%20-%20Attachments/Pasted%20image%2020260902165438.png&#34; alt=&#34;Pasted image 20260902165438.png&#34;  /&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Where the walls meet the floor, would want to use acoustic sealing and padding:&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;p class=&#34;imgp&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/ob/99%20-%20Attachments/Pasted%20image%2020260902165549.png&#34; alt=&#34;Pasted image 20260902165549.png&#34;  /&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Communicating Door</title>
				<link>//localhost:1313/posts/06---projects/house/basement/theater-construction/resources/communicating-door/</link>
				<pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 18:25:21 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>//localhost:1313/posts/06---projects/house/basement/theater-construction/resources/communicating-door/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;Notes from &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8Yep447wdzk%5c&amp;amp;t=110s&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noreferrer nofollow&#34;&gt;this Youtube video&lt;/a&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;1/16&amp;quot; thick rubber over gap between the walls:&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;p class=&#34;imgp&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/ob/99%20-%20Attachments/Pasted%20image%2020260908132526.png&#34; alt=&#34;Pasted image 20260908132526.png&#34;  /&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Door frame would look like this once built:&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;p class=&#34;imgp&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/ob/99%20-%20Attachments/Pasted%20image%2020260908132721.png&#34; alt=&#34;Pasted image 20260908132721.png&#34;  /&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Then place 1.6-3 PCF Mineral Wool along the gap:&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;p class=&#34;imgp&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/ob/99%20-%20Attachments/Pasted%20image%2020260908132823.png&#34; alt=&#34;Pasted image 20260908132823.png&#34;  /&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Then cover that the mineral wool with acoustic fabric.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;todo&#34;&gt;Todo&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;[ ] Will need contractor help/advice on how to approach this&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Isolation Clips</title>
				<link>//localhost:1313/posts/06---projects/house/basement/theater-construction/resources/isolation-clips/</link>
				<pubDate>Sun, 06 Sep 2026 19:33:35 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>//localhost:1313/posts/06---projects/house/basement/theater-construction/resources/isolation-clips/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;isolation-clips&#34;&gt;Isolation Clips&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I&amp;rsquo;ll use IB-1 isolation clips as seen &lt;a href=&#34;https://shop.soundproofingcompany.com/products/ib-1-soundproofing-clip?variant=33155367960711&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noreferrer nofollow&#34;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;p class=&#34;imgp&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/ob/99%20-%20Attachments/Pasted%20image%2020260902162555.png&#34; alt=&#34;Pasted image 20260902162555.png&#34;  /&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;hat-channels&#34;&gt;Hat Channels&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Required hat channel specifications for the clips. Can be purchased at most building supply stores.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Gauge: 25 Gauge (for its flexibilty)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unacceptable Gauge: 20 - (too stiff)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Required: Hemmed Long Edge&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Height: 7/8” (22.2 mm)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Length: 10&amp;rsquo; and 12&#39;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Thickness: .0188” (.478mm)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Designation Code: 087F125-18&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Acceptable Widths: 2 ½&amp;quot;, 2 9/16” and 2 5/8&amp;quot;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unacceptable width: channel larger than 2 3/4&amp;quot; is out of spec and not to be used.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Fasteners:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>HVAC</title>
				<link>//localhost:1313/posts/06---projects/house/basement/theater-construction/hvac/</link>
				<pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 01:46:05 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>//localhost:1313/posts/06---projects/house/basement/theater-construction/hvac/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;soffit&#34;&gt;Soffit&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Will need intake and return ducts for ventilation. Ventilation is a big escape path for sound, so will need to implement some soundproofing considerations here. One important thing will be to run flex+insulated ducting a good distance within the decoupled room. A longer duct will reduce sound transmission. Will want to keep the ducting WITHIN the decoupled room, likely in a soffit.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Good example for soffit construction here (Bigmouth Soffit build - &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.avsforum.com/posts/20844513/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noreferrer nofollow&#34;&gt;https://www.avsforum.com/posts/20844513/&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;p class=&#34;imgp&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/ob/99%20-%20Attachments/Pasted%20image%2020260908142416.png&#34; alt=&#34;Pasted image 20260908142416.png&#34;  /&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Electrical</title>
				<link>//localhost:1313/posts/06---projects/house/basement/theater-construction/electrical/</link>
				<pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 01:46:01 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>//localhost:1313/posts/06---projects/house/basement/theater-construction/electrical/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;projector&#34;&gt;Projector&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Grey PVC conduit to run wires to projector mount area&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;p class=&#34;imgp&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/ob/99%20-%20Attachments/Pasted%20image%2020260908141249.png&#34; alt=&#34;Pasted image 20260908141249.png&#34;  /&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;p class=&#34;imgp&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/ob/99%20-%20Attachments/Pasted%20image%2020260908141323.png&#34; alt=&#34;Pasted image 20260908141323.png&#34;  /&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Drywall</title>
				<link>//localhost:1313/posts/06---projects/house/basement/theater-construction/drywall/</link>
				<pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 01:45:54 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>//localhost:1313/posts/06---projects/house/basement/theater-construction/drywall/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;goal&#34;&gt;Goal&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Will use double 5/8&amp;quot; drywall with Green Glue (dampening compound) between the two layers on the walls and ceiling. This will provide mass and dampening for sound isolation (along with the decoupled framing of the room).  Diagram from the manufacturer showing the use on walls (would be the same for the ceiling):&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;p class=&#34;imgp&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/ob/99%20-%20Attachments/Pasted%20image%2020260906143755.png&#34; alt=&#34;Pasted image 20260906143755.png&#34;  /&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;First layer of ceiling drywall placed first. Drywall on soffit box (with Green Glue between drywall and OSB). Drywall on walls. Acoustic sealant at all seams/edges. SECOND layer of drywall on ceiling (WITH GREEN GLUE). SECOND layer of drywall on walls (WITH GREEN GLUE).&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;p class=&#34;imgp&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/ob/99%20-%20Attachments/Pasted%20image%2020260906145518.png&#34; alt=&#34;Pasted image 20260906145518.png&#34;  /&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Framing</title>
				<link>//localhost:1313/posts/06---projects/house/basement/theater-construction/framing/</link>
				<pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 01:45:49 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>//localhost:1313/posts/06---projects/house/basement/theater-construction/framing/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;goal&#34;&gt;Goal&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Overall, half of the proposed theater will have walls against foundation. The other half (the back of the theater) will have walls adjacent to a hallway to the guest room and to a large open entertainment space. My goal is to have some degree of sound isolation from the theater to the rest of the basement as well as upstairs. I hope to achieve this by having an independently framed &amp;ldquo;room within a room&amp;rdquo; for the theater space. This will result in having a double stud wall for the boundaries of the room that would share a connection with the other parts of the basement. For the boundaries adjacent to the foundation, this won&amp;rsquo;t be needed. The obvious constraints to the room are the concrete foundation and the support beams/columns. Here is the raw space I will be working with:&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;p class=&#34;imgp&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/ob/99%20-%20Attachments/Pasted%20image%2020260903122534.png&#34; alt=&#34;Pasted image 20260903122534.png&#34;  /&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Links</title>
